      "writtenOn": "2021-04-13T18:39:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve seen this happening on Oneplus sm8250 devices with R firmware.\nBut I can see from QCOM sm8250 BSP ( in Q ) they used this field in their custom network selection interface ( com.qualcomm.qti.networksetting ) that replaced AOSP V2 network selection ( or so I think ).\nNetworkSetting.apk for reference on any QCOM device.\n\nThen in R some devices moved back to AOSP network selection, thus QCOM didn\u0027t remove the extra field in some BSP releases and some devices end up with it on R still.\nEx Rog 3 uses AOSP, but OnePlus still uses NetworkSetting.\n\nAt the same time, setNetworkSelectionModeManual requires to append a \"+\" to operatorNumeric to successfully select the network.\nAt least they hacked both the getter and setter...\n\nIt\u0027s all speculation but BSP don\u0027t lie.",
      "parentUuid": "7926c12b_1281efe2",
